\begin{equation*}
1+c^{*}(S-1)=-\frac{\rho}{\phi\mu}S ,
\qquad 
c^{*}= \frac{-\rho S/\phi\mu-1}{S-1}\; .
\end{equation*}
Hence on the percolation form

\begin{equation*}
c^{*}= \frac{\kappa S-1}{S-1},
\end{equation*}
the dimensionless homeostatic control is the LTD offset normalised
by the mean pre-synaptic drive ${\rm E}[v_{k}]=\phi\mu$,

\begin{equation*}
\kappa\equiv-\frac{\rho}{\phi\mu}>0\qquad{\rm for\;the\;physiological}
\;\rho<0 ,
\end{equation*}
i.e. in magnitude

\begin{equation*}
|\kappa|=\frac{|\rho|}{\phi\mu}=\frac{|\rho|}{{\rm E}[v_{k}]},
\end{equation*}
so that $c^{*}\to\kappa$ for $S\to\infty$ and $c^{*}\to1$ for an isolated
synapse, $-\rho=\phi\mu$, $\kappa=1$, the usual LTP/LTD balance.
